% ============================================================================
% quadrilateral-secondary-property.query.adj — a worked recall over the
% geometry quadrilateral-secondary-property library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what else is true of a
% rectangle's sides, besides the right angles?": it states no geometry fact
% of its own — it only `import`s the grounded table and asks binding
% queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the
% `quadrilateral_secondary_property` rows and returns the secondary
% property + the table's source/locator/trust. A shape the cited spans give
% no second property for abstains honestly — the engine never invents one.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli quadrilateral-secondary-property.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "quadrilateral-secondary-property.adj"

? quadrilateral_secondary_property(rectangle, $Property)         % expect opposite_sides_equal_length
? quadrilateral_secondary_property($Shape, opposite_angles_equal) % reverse bind — expect parallelogram
? quadrilateral_secondary_property(square, $Property)             % expect abstain — square's own cited span names only one property, no second
